1. Executive Summary
This project is a web-based auto-grading application designed to evaluate student HTML/CSS websites against a standardized rubric. The system accepts a live URL, crawls all same-domain pages, validates HTML using the W3C Nu HTML Checker API, and scores the site across seven rubric categories, producing a 0–100 numeric grade with detailed feedback.

2. Project Objectives
Automate grading of student websites for structural, stylistic, and validation requirements.

Provide immediate feedback to students with actionable recommendations.

Ensure consistency across grading by applying objective, programmatic criteria.

Reduce instructor workload by eliminating manual HTML validation and structure checking.

3. Functional Requirements
3.1 Input
URL Input: User submits a single live URL (student's homepage, e.g., https://studentname.github.io/project1).

Validation: URL must be valid HTTP/HTTPS.

Scope: System crawls only same-domain pages (same scheme and hostname as root URL).

3.2 Crawling Behavior
Starting Point: Homepage URL provided by user.

Link Following:

Extract all <a href> links from each page.

Follow only internal links (same domain as root).

Ignore:

Fragments (#...)

mailto:, tel:, javascript: links

External domains

Depth & Limits:

Breadth-first crawl.

Cap at 30 HTML pages to prevent runaway crawling.

Normalize URLs (resolve relative paths, strip fragments).

Track visited URLs to avoid duplicates.

3.3 W3C HTML Validation
Service: W3C Nu HTML Checker API at https://validator.w3.org/nu/

Method: GET request with ?doc=<url>&out=json for each discovered HTML page.

Message Classification:

Errors: type == "error"

Warnings: type == "info" and subtype == "warning"

Info: Other informational messages (ignored for scoring)

Data Collected: For each message:

URL of page

Type and subtype

Message text

Line/column numbers

Extract (code snippet)

3.4 Page Analysis
For each HTML page, extract:

External Stylesheets: All <link rel="stylesheet" href="..."> references

Structural Elements:

Forms: <form> elements

Tables: <table> with <tr>, <th>, or <td>

Lists: <ul> or <ol> with <li>

Media: <img>, <video>, <audio>

Internal Links: All same-domain <a href> links

Inline/Internal Styles: Presence of <style> tags (noted but not penalized)

3.5 CSS Analysis (Future Enhancement)
Download external CSS files referenced by pages.

Search for @media rules indicating responsive design.

Track where @media appears (external vs inline).

4. Grading Rubric (0–100 Points)
4.1 Page Count (10 points)
Requirement: At least 5 distinct addressable HTML pages on the same domain.

Scoring:

≥5 pages: 10 points

4 pages: 7 points

3 pages: 4 points

2 pages: 2 points

1 page: 0 points

Auto-Check: Count unique HTML URLs successfully crawled.

4.2 External Stylesheet as Main Source of Style (15 points)
Requirements:

At least one external CSS file linked via <link rel="stylesheet">.

That stylesheet is used by the majority of pages (≥4 pages if site has 5 pages).

Inline and internal <style> allowed but should not dominate.

Scoring:

Main stylesheet used on all pages: 15 points

Main stylesheet used on ≥4 pages: 12 points

Used on 2–3 pages: 7 points

Used on ≤1 page or no external stylesheet: 0 points

Auto-Check:

Identify most commonly linked external stylesheet across all pages.

Count pages that reference it.

4.3 Required HTML Structures (30 points)
Requirements: Site must correctly use the following elements without validation errors:

Form (7.5 points)

At least one <form> element

No W3C errors related to form or its descendants

Table (7.5 points)

At least one <table> with <tr> and <th> or <td>

No W3C errors related to table structure

Lists (7.5 points)

At least one <ul> or <ol> with <li>

No W3C errors related to list elements

Media (7.5 points)

At least one <img>, <video>, or <audio>

No W3C errors related to media element

Scoring per sub-criterion:

Present with 0 related errors: 7.5 points

Present with 1–2 related errors: 4 points

Present with 3+ related errors: 2 points

Not present: 0 points

Auto-Check:

Detect presence of elements via HTML parsing.

Map validator error messages to elements by line number or extract text.

4.4 Responsiveness via @media (10 points)
Requirement: At least one @media rule in CSS for responsive design.

Scoring:

@media found in external stylesheet: 10 points

@media only in inline <style> tags: 6 points

No @media rules: 0 points

Auto-Check:

Download external CSS files.

Search for @media keyword followed by media query and rule block.

4.5 Consistent Theme via Shared External CSS (15 points)
Requirement: Majority of styling comes from a shared external stylesheet reused across pages.

Scoring:

Main stylesheet used on all pages: 15 points

Main stylesheet used on ≥4 pages: 12 points

Used on 2–3 pages: 5 points

Used on ≤1 page: 0 points

Auto-Check: Same as section 4.2 (reuse of main stylesheet).

4.6 Navigation & Internal Linking (10 points)
Requirements:

Site has navigable internal structure.

Internal links do not produce 404 errors.

At least 4 distinct internal links present across the site.

Scoring:

0 broken internal links and ≥4 internal links: 10 points

1–2 broken links: 7 points

3–5 broken links: 4 points

>5 broken links or minimal internal linking: 0 points

Auto-Check:

Collect all internal links from crawled pages.

Attempt HTTP requests to each and track status codes.

Count links returning non-2xx/3xx responses as broken.

