7. Non-Functional Requirements
7.1 Performance
Crawl Time: Maximum 30 seconds for sites with ≤30 pages

Validation: W3C API calls may take 1–3 seconds per page; timeout at 20 seconds per request

Concurrency: Async HTTP requests to improve speed

Rate Limiting: Respect W3C validator usage guidelines (avoid excessive requests)

7.2 Reliability
Error Handling:

If a page fails to load (404, timeout), skip and continue crawling

If W3C validator fails for a page, note in details but continue grading other criteria

Graceful Degradation: Partial scores awarded based on successfully analyzed pages

7.3 Usability
Simple GUI: Single-page interface with URL input and grade display

Clear Feedback: Students see:

Total score (large, prominent)

Per-section breakdown

Specific issues and recommendations

Fast Feedback Loop: Results returned within 30–60 seconds

7.4 Security
Input Validation: Pydantic validates URL format

No Arbitrary Code Execution: Only fetch and parse HTML/CSS (no JavaScript execution)

Rate Limiting (future): Prevent abuse by limiting requests per IP/user

7.5 Maintainability
Modular Design: Separate concerns (crawling, validation, scoring)

Clear Documentation: Inline comments and README

Extensible Rubric: Easy to adjust point values or add new criteria

