12. Constraints and Assumptions
12.1 Constraints
No JavaScript Execution: Crawler does not execute JavaScript (static HTML analysis only)

W3C API Dependency: Grading relies on external W3C validator service availability

Same-Domain Only: Cannot grade multi-domain student projects

Page Limit: Maximum 30 pages to prevent excessive crawl times

12.2 Assumptions
Students host sites on public URLs (GitHub Pages, Netlify, etc.)

Sites use standard HTML5 and CSS3

Students understand and accept automated grading limitations

Instructor has access to Linux server or LXC environment for deployment

13. Glossary
W3C Nu HTML Checker: Official HTML5 validator service (validator.w3.org/nu/)

Same-Domain Link: URL with matching scheme and hostname as root URL

Internal Link: Same as same-domain link (used interchangeably)

External Stylesheet: CSS file linked via <link rel="stylesheet">

Inline Style: CSS in <style> tags or style attributes

Validator Message: Error, warning, or info message from W3C validator

Rubric: Grading criteria with point allocations (0–100 scale)

